From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mariotaku <git@mariotaku.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] linux-user: vendor netlink families passed through

socket(AF_NETLINK, ..., protocol) was refused with EPROTONOSUPPORT for
every protocol but NETLINK_ROUTE, NETLINK_KOBJECT_UEVENT and
NETLINK_AUDIT. webOS's Bluetooth service learns that its MediaTek adapter
is plugged in from the driver's own family (29), so under qemu-arm it
never powered the adapter on.

Families above NETLINK_SMC (22), which no mainline subsystem uses, are
now created and their messages passed unchanged. That holds for messages
without pointer- or long-sized fields, as nlmsghdr and the MediaTek
driver's registration and state messages are. Mainline's other families
are still refused.
---
diff --git a/linux-user/syscall.c b/linux-user/syscall.c
--- a/linux-user/syscall.c
+++ b/linux-user/syscall.c
@@ -3170,6 +3170,17 @@
     return fd;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The netlink families after mainline's last (NETLINK_SMC, 22) are a vendor driver's own, such
+ * as MediaTek's Bluetooth driver's (btmtk_usb: 29 or 30), which webOS's Bluetooth service opens
+ * to learn the adapter's USB state. Their messages pass unchanged, with no translator: that is
+ * right only for messages without pointer- or long-sized fields, whose layout is then the same
+ * for a 32-bit ARM guest and a 64-bit host. The ones known hold that: nlmsghdr (a u32, two
+ * u16, two u32) followed by MediaTek's registration (the string "btmngr") and its state
+ * replies (two int32). Mainline's other families stay refused, as before.
+ */
+#define NETLINK_VENDOR_MIN 23
+
 /* do_socket() Must return target values and target errnos. */
 static abi_long do_socket(int domain, int type, int protocol)
 {
@@ -3186,7 +3197,8 @@
          protocol == NETLINK_ROUTE ||
 #endif
          protocol == NETLINK_KOBJECT_UEVENT ||
-         protocol == NETLINK_AUDIT)) {
+         protocol == NETLINK_AUDIT ||
+         protocol >= NETLINK_VENDOR_MIN)) {
         return -TARGET_EPROTONOSUPPORT;
     }
 
@@ -3217,7 +3229,9 @@
                 fd_trans_register(ret, &target_netlink_audit_trans);
                 break;
             default:
-                g_assert_not_reached();
+                /* a vendor family (above): its messages pass unchanged */
+                g_assert(protocol >= NETLINK_VENDOR_MIN);
+                break;
             }
         }
     }
